  <ym-title|Chapter 15 audit><label|chapter-15-audit>

  <section|Source use and original literature><label|source-use-and-original-literature>

  Read Scott/part2/H-section.tex:1\U190, Martin/existence/phase-selection.tex:1\U185
  and phases.tex:109\U285. The text follows the ground-space compression
  construction, retaining whole-word Gram operators, the additional real
  bounded-approximation hypothesis for phase reflection, corrected all-copy
  detector moments, and the almost-everywhere qualification for the ground
  line.

  Original Gelfand\UNeumark (1943), Ÿ2 Lemma 1, read from Mathnet publisher
  scan, proves the commutative isometric representation needed here. Landsman
  (1998) is the arXiv lecture notes math-ph/9807030, not the separate book;
  original PDF checked for the commutative representation, positivity and
  state/measure theorems (Ÿ2.6 and Theorems 2.4.1, 2.8.2). Standard
  C*-algebra and Riesz arguments are cited rather than reproved.

  <section|Actual construction dependencies
  retained><label|actual-construction-dependencies-retained>

  <\enumerate>
    <item>Chapter14 Euclidean covariance, slab norm smoothness and normalized
    Ward laws retain their stated marked comparison and annular hypotheses.

    <item>The bounded real approximants in the phase-reflection variance
    argument must be supplied for the same Wilson family, uniformly in copy
    position; cutoff, large separation, copy number and approximation-error
    limits have the stated order.

    <item>Corrected detector errors need all-copy moment estimates. A small
    mixed expectation alone does not imply uniform character estimates or
    equality of field null spaces.

    <item>No uniqueness in every phase or point-mass decomposition is
    asserted here. The retained phase is selected from one common
    full-measure set using a countable dense word family.
  </enumerate>

  <section|Review><label|review>

  Independent review completed in chapter-15-independent-review.md. Both
  generic-grid and bounded-reference-mean repairs applied. Integrated
  compilation passed and all Chapter15 pages visually reviewed in the
  177-page checkpoint.
